WEBVTT

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.180
Please. Let me stay here!

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.290
I'll do anything.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.530
Please let me work here.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.780
<i>Anything</i>?

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.030
Y-Yes.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.160
Are you sure?

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.310
I-I'm sure.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.350
This job is pretty rough.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.610
I'll work hard.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.020
Wait around till we close.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.690
<b>Mom</b>

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.940
Thanks for waiting.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:12.650
What?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.150
This way.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.300
I'm the director, 
but just over summer break.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.660
Otherwise, my gramps is supposed 
to be the director.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.380
I need to ask Gramps and Grams.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.920
Sure.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.170
I thought you'd say so.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.610
You can stay at our place.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.140
You're so quick 
to let people stay here.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.300
Sheesh.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.630
Fuuka-chan, huh?

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:47.050
Fuuka's a word for big sharks.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.240
Did you know that?

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.950
Are you hungry?

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.720
Want some Okinawan doughnuts?

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.440
Oh, don't mind me.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.580
And you always try 
to keep everyone fed, Grams.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.460
Right?

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.070
I'm such a people-pleaser.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.100
I'll help.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.280
Gramps,

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.920
you met the new—

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.290
They said they'll take in a few for us.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.290
I don't want to give up yet.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.760
I'm surprised your parents
let you do a live-in job.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.070
Oh, um...

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.390
Here, try this.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.710
Oh, it's all right.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.860
Just try it.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.900
Okay, thank you.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.110
Thanks.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.200
It's good!

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.620
It's got purple yam inside, 
which makes it green.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.310
You're right.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:09.640
Hello?

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:10.540
<i>Fuuka?!</i>

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.920
<i>I was so worried!</i>

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.590
<i>You wouldn't answer the phone.</i>

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:15.800
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.240
I told you. My friend's place.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.770
<i>Which friend? And where?</i>

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.740
I told you. My group members put on 
a farewell party for me.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.660
And I stayed over at Ruka-chan's place.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:31.660
Grams, I'm supposed to meet someone. 
I'll see you later.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.210
Sure.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.710
Good evening.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.430
Welcome.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.040
<b>Kameichi</b>

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.550
<b>Kameichi Diner</b>

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.550
What about money?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.080
I'll figure it out.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.130
Have you told your grams?

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.090
No.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.060
They're definitely going to say no.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.510
I'm sure they would.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.130
But I've already made up my mind.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.020
What's up? 
Are you scheming something?

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:54.570
No way.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.130
It's about Kukuru's big summer plans.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.040
Oh?

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.020
An elementary-school research project?

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.230
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.610
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium cold water 
filter tank upgrade</b>

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.030
<b>Gakefuchi Industries Co.</b>

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:00.840
<b>Quote</b>

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.240
I want to replace some broken tank parts.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.190
I had some estimates done.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.530
<b>Gakefuchi Industries Co.</b>

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.530
<b>Construction fee</b>

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.530
<b>Miscellaneous expenditures</b>

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.530
<b>Total</b>

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:10.030
One, ten, hundred, thousand, ten thousand...

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.400
Where are you going 
to get all this money?!

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.080
I'll figure it out.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.530
I'll work really hard over the summer 
to bring in lots of customers.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.540
Are you sure you can bring in 
so many so quickly?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.620
I'll make it work.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.430
This summer is my last chance.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.590
If you make summer event flyers, 
we'll hand them out for you.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.310
Is that all right, Mom?

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.310
Sure, go ahead.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:39.770
She's hopeless.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.200
She's drunk already.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.000
What about her fortune telling?

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.210
Only when her drinking buddies aren't around.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.080
What a laid-back lifestyle, huh?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.160
Meanwhile, she has her daughter 
take care of the shop.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:50.700
Oh, yeah.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.370
I took a customer to Gama Gama today.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.700
A super pretty girl who seemed 
to be going through some things.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.640
Oh, that's Miyazawa-san.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.920
She's going to be living in at my place 
and working at the aquarium.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.170
"Living in"?!

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.170
Yeah.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.720
Now that we have more staff, 
we can put on more events, too.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.290
I'm going to make it happen.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.300
This summer's going to be all about work!

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:22.000
You'll have to bear with the lack of space.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.150
Thanks.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.110
Can I ask you something?

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.070
Sure.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.240
Where were you going to go 
if you couldn't work for us?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.430
Anywhere.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.640
Oh.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.200
It didn't have to be an aquarium, huh?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.100
You're in high school, aren't you?

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.250
Where do you live?

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.760
Do I have to answer that?

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.470
Well, whatever.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.090
Although, as the summer director, 
I'm curious.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.880
I'm sorry.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.980
Good morning.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:02.230
I'd like to introduce you all 
to a new member of our team today.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.280
What? "You all"?

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.470
This is Yakamashi Kuuya-san, 
one of our attendants.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:09.080
I'm Miyazawa Fuuka.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.610
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.610
Hey.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:17.000
There's also Gramps, who's the aquarium director, 
and Umi-yan, another attendant.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.440
But Gramps is out on business 
a lot lately.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.240
Umi-yan is on break with a bad back.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:25.680
My shifts seriously suck.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:30.080
Miyazawa-san's going to be living with us 
and working here for a while.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.260
Huh.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.140
I can't with girls.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.640
I'm going to go look around.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.140
Nope, nope, nope.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.000
Kuuya-san has a hard time around girls.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.310
Be gentle with him.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.650
Right...

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.770
We also have a vet who comes in.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.490
I'll introduce you to them when we see them.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.430
Okay.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.040
Use these for now.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.240
Got it.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:57.980
Smells like fish.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:07:59.120
No way!

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.760
No, no, never!

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:01.540
Nail polish?!

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:03.950
Don't put anything on your skin!

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.720
No perfume or cosmetics, either!

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.610
This is all for the sake 
of the plants and animals!

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:08.510
Remove it all!

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:09.550
Clean yourself off!

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:11.470
Okay.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.130
Sorry.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.380
No.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.560
I forgot to tell you, too.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.790
Just learn everything one at a time.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:19.830
Okay.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:23.920
We're going to be feeding 
the penguins later today.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.370
Can you help out?

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:26.400
Okay.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:32.120
We feed them horse mackerel, 
defrosted in running water.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.340
That's Umi-yan's personal stuff.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:38.910
<b>Do Not Eat</b>

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:36.750
Shochu-infused ice pops.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.910
"Shochu-infused"...

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:45.780
We put vitamins in the gills 
before we feed them to the penguins.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.170
The fish's nutritional value gets lost 
when we defrost it.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.630
So we're supplementing them.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.130
Huh.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:57.050
The guests love feeding time.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.280
I'll take care of running the event.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.730
When I give you the signal, 
feed them from the head, like this.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.050
I'll back you up, since it's your first time.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.780
G-Got it.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.240
Welcome, everyone!

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:17.690
I see that we have even more kids than usual, 
now that it's summer break.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:22.400
I'd like to present to you 
the penguins' feeding time.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.200
In this bucket, we have horse mackerel.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.460
I haven't seen her here before.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.840
Which one?

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:28.810
Her.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.910
Hurry! Hurry!

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:40.400
Ow!

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.140
Surprised, everyone?!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:46.140
Penguin beaks are quite sharp. 
Feeding them can be...

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.720
Wait...

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.150
Ow!

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.060
Stop!

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.400
Stop pinching!

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.180
I never said you could have that!

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.040
No!

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.950
No, no, no!

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.580
No!

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:20.720
You...

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.970
<b>Getting Wet Is Part Of the Job</b>

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.030
You can't be serious.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.230
I can't blame you, 
since this was your first time.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:28.620
Right.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.730
I'm sorry.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.660
The highest priority at an aquarium 
is the safety of the plants and animals.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:34.610
You understand, don't you?

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.860
If something goes wrong, 
it's already too late.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:43.450
Hey, when you said you wanted this job, 
did you even care what it was?

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:49.650
Don't forget that you're in charge of
the animals' lives, and that they're precious.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.560
Protect them with everything you've got.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.230
That's what I've been taught.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:11:00.940
I'm sorry, but if something happens 
to our animals, I won't forgive you.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.790
I'm sorry.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.240
Never mind the animals.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.440
Can you wash the tanks?

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.180
Okay.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.240
Ow...

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:28.890
I'm the worst.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:47.290
D-Do what's right,

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:52.270
and everything will work out.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.540
Did I get that right?

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:04.750
Don't forget to put this board out 
when we open in the morning.

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:05.510
Okay.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:11.660
<b>Welcome to Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.650
This is cute.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:09.870
Thanks.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:11.660
We're a small aquarium.

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:15.900
I wanted to be sincere 
in welcoming our guests.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.790
<i>Sincere, huh?</i>

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:22.060
What should I do next?

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:24.440
Could you clean the front door, please?

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:26.190
Wash it down a little.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:27.210
Got it.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:29.310
Hello there.

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:31.810
Is the director here?

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.150
Yes, that's me.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.040
Hey, from the other day.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:57.670
Kukuru was really happy 
that she has a new member on staff.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.550
Although I'm on the verge of getting fired.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.140
I see.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:08.910
Yes.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.780
I really screwed up.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:17.900
I think Kukuru was just really angry 
because she's struggling, too.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:25.210
This place might be closing soon.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:28.170
Gama Gama was about to go bust,

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:32.240
when Kukuru's grandpa took over 
and kept it running until now.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:38.630
<b>Welcome to Gama Gama</b>

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.020
The equipment's getting really old.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.090
You know how there's a ton 
of machinery behind aquariums?

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:42.300
Apparently, it's going to cost 
a lot of money to keep it going.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.100
I never knew.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.890
Gramps had decided he'd close shop 
at the end of summer and retire.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:53.640
But Kukuru hasn't given up.

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.840
Gama Gama Aquarium is her dream.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.900
She's trying to hold on to her dream?

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:06.730
So I think she's up against a wall.

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:08.040
I'm sorry.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.280
I'd appreciate if you could cut her some slack.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:15.290
I want to be of as much help as I can, too.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.510
I know how she feels.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:20.170
I don't want her to suffer.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.170
Thanks.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.960
<b>Naze Nantarou</b>

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.960
<b>Arama Daikichi</b>

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:26.780
We happened to hear 
that you might be closing.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.180
We thought you could use a hand.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:32.800
We could supply you 
with the money you need right away.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.290
The money I need?

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.010
No problem if you're underage, either.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:41.210
We have our ways of making it work.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:42.200
Right?

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.070
We aren't closing.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.440
Please leave.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:49.700
I'm here to pick up leaflets.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:53.100
I thought I'd hand them out at
the upcoming Tourism Association event.

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.210
I think I saw some extra at reception.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:59.930
I thought it'd be an easy day, 
selling to a kid.

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:02.210
What a lousy director.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.410
She's just a high-school kid.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:06.710
She should just take the money.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.450
It's just some brat running it for fun.

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:13.090
This aquarium's going under in no time.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:19.610
Huh, was someone here?

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.020
I'm going to go spread some salt!

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.650
What the hell are you doing?

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:27.600
Damn.

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:28.650
Awful.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.120
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.930
I'll pay for it.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:37.840
How much is it?

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.320
You're so low.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:40.370
Wha?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.830
You're so low!

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.280
Go away!

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:47.820
I don't want you here anymore 
if you don't know how valuable this board is!

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:49.560
Go away!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.860
Never come back!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.240
You're a piece of shit!

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.210
Enjoy losing your jobs!

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:00.410
No way...

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:15.370
I'm sorry for acting out of turn!

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:21.500
As the director, I find it inexcusable 
that you would spray water at a visitor,

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.220
whoever they may be.

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:25.590
You'd be fired immediately.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.060
On the other hand...

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.160
Well, they weren't customers.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.620
And I feel better.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.510
Thanks.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:37.720
Thank goodness.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:41.020
I thought I'd be working non-stop again.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.250
I'm actually going to die.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.260
Come on. Seriously.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.260
You make it sound so serious.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.380
Hey, Kukuru, I'll call Udon-chan.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.060
Let's hold a welcome party tonight.

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:51.050
It's fine.

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:52.330
Don't worry.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:53.930
We're all bored in the countryside.

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:55.290
Meet up at seven.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:56.820
Are you sure?

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.020
She's just looking for an excuse to drink.

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:00.330
You can turn her down.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.090
You're coming, too!

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:03.830
There's no way.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.570
Maybe I'll bring Grams's plum wine.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:08.180
Karin-chan will appreciate it.

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.890
Grams's plum wine...

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:17.380
And then Fuuka-chan here 
sprayed them down with the hose!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:18.970
I'm sorry.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:21.180
Why? That was awesome!

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.100
Huh?

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.120
You're here, too, Kai?

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:25.960
Kuuya-san invited me.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:28.160
He dragged me in, 
because he didn't want it to be all girls.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.310
Cheers!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.840
Are you drinking your juice, Kai-kun?

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:35.280
Man, the booze is better when you're
drinking with good-looking guys.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.470
You're so generous when you're drunk.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:39.740
And you don't remember any of it.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.660
Have you all introduced yourselves yet?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.670
Yes.

00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:43.740
Um...

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:45.790
Karin-san, of the Tourism Association.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.950
Kai-kun, who's in the same grade 
as the director.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.540
This is Udon-chan.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.420
She's the poster girl for this shop, 
and my classmate.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.860
"Udon-chan"?

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:58.680
Her name's Tsukimi, so she's Udon-chan, 
as in <i>tsukimi udon</i>.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:17:59.660
That's right.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.630
Nice to meet you, Fuuka-chan.

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:03.520
How long are you staying over here?

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.800
For as long as I can.

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:09.930
We're able to fill our shifts for a while, 
but with Umi-yan and Gramps gone,

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:12.720
we don't have enough guys for heavy lifting.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:14.900
Should I help?

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.510
Just for summer break, right?

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:22.830
I'll be helping with my dad's work 
in the mornings, but I'll be free after.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:23.950
If that's good enough.

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.940
Kai! Yes, please!

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:27.620
Starting when?

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.670
Tomorrow.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:29.560
What?!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.080
Fine.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:32.880
Good luck.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.070
You said you needed help, so—

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:36.630
You're doing it for me?!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.200
Kai-kun!

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.700
Kuuya-san?!

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.640
All right, I'm feeling pumped.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.900
One more, please!

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:44.390
<b>Kameichi Diner</b>

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.500
Um...

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.550
About Gama Gama Aquarium...

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:57.660
Yeah...

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.910
Sorry I never told you about it closing.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:02.570
It's okay.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.440
Karin-san told me.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:08.860
Also that you're betting your summer on it.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:10.360
Yeah.

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:15.210
I love Gama Gama Aquarium.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.850
This is my home.

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:19.470
My special place.

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:23.820
My dream is to protect it forever.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.530
I just have to do what I can right now.

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:41.620
There's something I want to tell you, too.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:47.180
I ran away here, 
after I got fired as an idol.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:56.060
I had a dream since I was a kid. 
I moved to Tokyo when I was

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:57.960
in middle school to make it happen.

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.970
I was in the corner of my group 
when I first made my debut,

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:05.400
but I was finally as a candidate 
to be in the center.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
<b>New song:</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
<b>Love Clover</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
<b>Center:</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
<b>Miyazawa Fuuka</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
<b>Subs:</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
<b>Shiroi Ruka</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
<b>Miyamori Aoi</b>

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.320
But then...

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.250
My grandma hasn't been doing too well.

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:13.290
This concert might be my last chance!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:14.940
But...

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.860
Please! Just this once!

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:19.830
Please let me have the next concert.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:24.430
I gave it some thought, and gave up 
my opportunity to be in the center.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:26.870
I gave my chance to a newer member.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:32.280
I guess the manager and staff 
thought I was being lazy.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:37.060
I lost more and more work after that.

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:39.820
They told me maybe
it was time to call it quits,

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:42.220
especially since I'm graduating 
high school this year.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.650
Time to call it quits?

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:46.890
I got fired.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:50.040
My dream ended.

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.880
I ended up here after all that,

00:20:56.660 --> 00:21:00.680
and actually, I haven't even told
my parents where I am right now.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:02.240
You're a runaway?!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.280
I'll let them know once I settle down.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:08.640
That's pretty heavy, Miyazawa-san.

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:10.710
I think so, too.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.920
Thanks for telling me.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:24.470
I feel a little better, too, 
now that I've opened up.

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:29.930
May I stay here?

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:34.990
I didn't care where I went at first.

00:21:34.990 --> 00:21:37.190
But now, it's different.

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:43.190
My dream's over, but I can
still support someone's dream.

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:46.390
I don't want you to give up, Director.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:54.820
You can call me "Kukuru."

00:21:55.630 --> 00:21:58.960
Help me with my dream, Fuuka.
